.TH SHMMEM 1 "2026-11-08" "ShmMem 2.3" "Gambas Components"
.SH NAME
shmmem \- Gambas 3 component for sharing variables between tasks and applications in Linux shared memory
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B Dim mymem As New ShmMem("segment_name")
.BI "Dim mymem As New ShmMem(" length ", " name ", " max_symbols ", " lock_timeout ", " executable ", " permissions ")"
.B mymem!myvar = 100
.B Print mymem!myvar
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ShmMem
stores Gambas values in Linux shared memory, so that tasks and applications on the same machine can read and
change them directly, without copying them through the kernel.
Any value that Gambas can write with
.B Write As Variant
can be stored: native values, arrays, collections and objects.
Variables do not need to be declared before use, and their type may change, except while another task is
notified of their changes.
.PP
A segment has a symbol table and a variable memory area.
Values are reached by name:
.BR mymem!name ,
.B mymem["name"]
or
.BR mymem.name .
.PP
A named segment can be used by every application with the right permissions.
An unnamed segment, made with an empty name, is shared by the application and its tasks only.
The segments are deleted when the last task or application using them closes.
.SH CREATING A SEGMENT
.TP
.I length
Size of the variable memory in bytes. Defaults to 20000000 (20 MB).
.TP
.I name
Name of the segment. Two segments are made in /dev/shm:
.IB name _Data
and
.IB name _Symbols .
An empty name makes an unnamed segment.
.TP
.I max_symbols
Maximum number of symbols. Defaults to 8000.
.TP
.I lock_timeout
Defaults to 0.1. Kept in the memory block and used by
.BR ExclusiveTimeout .
The normal lock waits up to 30 seconds, see
.BR LOCKS .
.TP
.I executable
Allows binary code in the segment to be run, see
.BR ShmThread .
Defaults to False.
.TP
.I permissions
Permissions of the segment. Defaults to &O660, or &O770 when executable.
.PP
All the parameters are optional.
.B New ShmMem("name")
uses the defaults for the rest.
.SH METHODS
.SS Variables
.TP
.BI Exist( name ") As Boolean"
True when the symbol exists.
.TP
.BI Remove( name )
Removes the symbol and frees its value. Tasks waiting for its removal are notified.
.TP
.BI Free( name )
Frees the symbol and the memory used by its value.
.TP
.BI Clear( "" "[ignore_list]" )
Removes every variable except those in ignore_list. Names starting with # are kept.
.TP
.BI Variables( "" "[filter]" ") As String[]"
Names of the variables that match the pattern filter, default "*".
.TP
.BI SizeOf( value ") As Long"
Storage size of a value.
.TP
.BI VarPtr( name ) ", VarEntryPtr(" name )
Virtual address of the value, and of the variable control block.
.SS Images and saved variables
Files are kept in
.B DefaultDirectory
(~/vars) unless a path is given.
.TP
.BI SaveImage( "" "[file]" )
Saves all the symbols and their values. Default file:
.IR application_name .image.
.TP
.BI LoadImage( "" "[file], [merge]" )
Loads a saved image. With merge set to True, variables that exist already are kept.
.TP
.BI MergeImage( "" "[file]" )
Same as LoadImage with merge set to True.
.TP
.BI SaveVar( name ", [file])"
Saves one variable, by default to
.IR name .var.
.TP
.BI LoadVar( file ", [name], [merge])"
Loads one variable, optionally under another name.
.TP
.BI SaveNativeVar( name ", " value ", [file])"
Saves a Gambas value as a variable file, without storing it in the segment.
.TP
.BI SetPath( path ", [base_name], [extension]) As String"
Full path of an image or variable file, with the defaults applied.
.SS Notifications
The handler is called with the variable name, the new value and a timed out flag.
.TP
.BI Notify( name ", " object ", [method], [timeout], [tag])"
Calls the handler when the variable changes. The variable must exist. The default handler is
.IR name _notify.
A timeout of 0 waits for ever.
.TP
.BI NotifyStop( name ", " object ", [method], [tag])"
Cancels a Notify request; name, object, method and tag must match it. Raises an error when no request matches.
.TP
.BI NotifyOnAny( enabled ", " object ", [method])"
Calls the handler when any variable changes.
.TP
.BI NotifyOnNew( enabled ", " object ", [method])"
Calls the handler when a variable is created.
.TP
.BI NotifyOnRemove( enabled ", " object ", [method])"
Calls the handler when a variable is removed.
.TP
.BI NotifyQ( name ") As ShmList"
The tasks and applications waiting for changes of the variable.
.PP
Each process waiting for notifications has a queue in the segment and a pipe,
.RI /dev/shm/shmmem-notify- pid .
The event is raised when the program returns to the Gambas event loop, for example in a
.BR Wait .
A busy program gets its events when it next creates, changes or removes a variable.
No signals are used.
.SS Waiting (deprecated, use the notifications)
.TP
.BI WaitFor( name ", [timeout]) As Boolean"
Waits for the variable to be created.
.TP
.BI WaitForValue( name ", " value ", [timeout]) As Boolean"
Waits for the variable to have the value.
.TP
.BI WaitValueChange( name ", " value ", [timeout]) As Boolean"
Waits for the variable to change from the value.
.PP
They check in a loop that pauses 1 ms at first, doubling up to 50 ms. A timeout of 0 waits for ever.
.SS Memory and segments
.TP
.BI Alloc( length ") As Pointer"
Allocates memory in the segment and returns its virtual address.
.TP
.BI RealAddress( virtual ") , RealDataAddress(" virtual )
Real address of a block, and of its data.
.TP
.B Close()
Closes the segment and releases its resources. Call it when the application ends.
.TP
.BI "ShmMem.ForceDelete(" name )
Deletes the segments of that name. Tasks still using them are left in a bad state.
.TP
.BI "ShmMem.GetMemSegment(" signature ") As ShmMem"
The open segment with that signature, used when objects are read back.
.TP
.BI "ShmMem.GetListType(" memory ", " type ") As Variant[]"
All the memory blocks of one datatype.
.TP
.BI "ShmMem.GetObjectClass(" object ") As Class"
The class of an object.
.SS Debugging
.TP
.BR Print() ", " PrintAllInfo( [title] ) ", " PrintTree()
Print the symbols, the memory information and blocks, and the hash buckets (not implemented).
.TP
.BI "ShmMem.Dump(" pointer ", " length ", [file])"
Writes memory to a file, by default ~/Desktop/dumpfile.ghex.
.SH PROPERTIES
.TP
.B Count, Length
Number of symbols.
.TP
.B Max, Key
The last index and the current name while iterating with For Each.
.TP
.B Debug
Turns debug messages on or off.
.TP
.B DefaultDirectory
Directory for images and variable files. Defaults to ~/vars.
.TP
.B Signature
Unique identifier of the ShmMem object, used to put values read back in the right segment.
.TP
.B ShmObjects
The open segments.
.TP
.B Version
The library version.
.TP
.B ShmMem.Objects, ShmMem.PID
Static: the open segments of this process, and its process id.
.SH DATATYPES
Shared datatypes keep their structure in the segment, so every task sees the same list, queue or array.
Create them with the segment they belong to, for example
.BR "New ShmList(mymem, 0, True, \(dqtag\(dq)" .
A tag, or the virtual address, refers to an existing one from another task.
.TP
.B ShmList
Doubly linked list with extended ids and tags.
.TP
.B ShmQueue
Queue, optionally ordered by priority.
.TP
.BR ShmFiFo ", " ShmFiLo
First in first out, and first in last out queues.
.TP
.B ShmArray
Static array of up to 10 dimensions.
.TP
.B ShmValue
A single value, found by tag, outside the symbol table.
.TP
.B ShmThread
Runs position independent binary code stored in an executable segment as a thread.
.TP
.B ShmStorableClass
Base class for your own classes: their public variables and properties are stored and read back.
Every public property must be writable.
.SH EXECUTABLE BLOCKS
A segment created with
.I executable
set to True can hold binary code, a blob written in assembler or C, and run it as a native thread inside the
program with
.BR ShmThread .
The code runs with no checks: a bad blob crashes the whole program.
.PP
.nf
smem = New ShmMem(1280000, "test", 3000, 2.2, True)
smem!a = File.Load("templates/pthreadPassString.bin")
Dim t As New ShmThread(smem, "a")
t.Execute("Hello\(rsn")         ' waits for the thread
.fi
.PP
.B Execute(\fIarg\fP, \fIWaitToComplete\fP)
starts the code at the first byte of the blob, with
.I arg
in register rdi: the address of a string's characters, a number, or
.B Object.Data()
of a structure whose first field is, by convention, the result.
With
.I WaitToComplete
set to False, call
.B WaitComplete()
before reading what the thread writes.
.PP
A blob must be x86-64 position independent code with its entry point at its first byte. It is not linked to any
library: it uses Linux system calls only, and keeps its data inside the blob. It ends with the exit system call
(60), never exit_group (231), which ends the whole program.
.PP
The
.B templates
directory of the project has blobs in assembler (pthreadPassString.asm, pthreadPassValue.asm,
pthreadPassStruct.asm) and C (pthreadStruct.c), with their build scripts:
.TP
.B ./buildAsm
Assembles the assembler templates into flat binaries with
.BR fasm (1).
.TP
.B ./buildC
Builds pthreadStruct.bin with
.B gcc -fPIE -fno-stack-protector
and
.B ld -T linkinfo
at address 0, keeps only the code with
.BR objcopy ,
and writes a disassembly to C_dump.txt.
In C the entry function must come first in the file, and there can be no global variables or string constants.
.PP
The example Examples/vTestApps/Executable_Shared_Segments/TestExecutableBlocks.module runs all the templates;
run it from the project directory after building them.
.SH LOCKS
The memory block, every list and queue, and every array have their own lock: a process shared, robust, recursive
pthread mutex in the segment.
.IP \(bu 2
A lock held by a process that ended or was killed is taken over by the next process that locks it, with the message
"a process ended while it held the lock of ..., recovered" on stderr. What that process was changing may be half done.
.IP \(bu 2
A process waits up to 30 seconds for a lock held by a live process, then the error
"Mutex race condition !!! : ..." is raised. Lists and arrays wait the Wait_Time of their Lock method.
.IP \(bu 2
Waiting does not use the processor: the waiters sleep in the kernel until the lock is released.
.IP \(bu 2
A process may take the same lock more than once; each Lock needs its Unlock.
.SH TASKS
A forked Task inherits the ShmMem objects of its parent. When the Task ends it does not change the use counts of its
parent's segment, lists and values, nor take over its notify queue. Lock counts are kept per process.
.SH ERRORS
Errors are raised to the caller; the library does not stop or print and carry on. Errors inside the library say
"internal error" and where. Examples: "Empty List - ..." when a list remove finds nothing, "Out Of Bounds",
"Out Of Variable Memory".
.SH FILES
.TP
.IB name _Data ", " name _Symbols
The two segments of a named ShmMem, in /dev/shm.
.TP
.RI /dev/shm/shmmem-notify- pid
The notify pipe of a process. A pipe left by a process that ended is removed by the next one that opens its pipe.
.TP
.RI ~/vars/ application .image
Default image file.
.SH NOTES
Segments made by a version before 2.3 use semaphores and can not be used with this version. Delete them with
.B ShmMem.ForceDelete
or remove their files in /dev/shm before starting.
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
Public Sub Main()

    Dim mymem As New ShmMem("mymem")

    mymem!counter = 0               ' Notify needs the variable to exist
    mymem.Notify("counter", Me, "Changed")
    mymem!counter = 1
    Wait 1                          ' events arrive in the event loop
    mymem.NotifyStop("counter", Me, "Changed")
    mymem.Close()

End

Public Sub Changed(VarName As String, Value As Variant, TimedOut As Boolean)

    Print VarName; " = "; Value

End
.fi
